          //   dock via a native transform against an existing element, and among
          //   clash-free candidates prefer the one that packs against the MOST distinct
          //   partners — this buries the helix in the core and, crucially, lets it
          //   contact sequence-distant elements (the chain folds back → long-range
          //   contacts). We do NOT bias the crossing angle: the teacher-forced control
          //   showed partner-maximization alone keeps the angle distribution native
